# ============================================================
# LAW #1 — NEVER UNDO. ONLY UPGRADE AND ADD.  (THE MOST IMPORTANT RULE)
# ============================================================
# This is an established site: ~60 hand-built core pages + programmatic clusters
# (/aeo/*, /industries/[industry], /malta/[location]/*), representing MONTHS of work.
# The owner has confirmed: design + content are GOOD. The gap is technical SEO + AEO depth.
#
# - NEVER rebuild, rewrite, or regenerate an existing page wholesale.
# - NEVER delete existing content to "clean it up." Preserve it.
# - When upgrading a page: READ it first, preserve what's there, ADD the missing brain layer
#   (Hero 1/2/3 depth, AEO Q&A, schema, internal links) SURGICALLY.
# - Every change must be a small, reviewable diff. Mostly green (additions), minimal red (a weak
#   line swapped for a strong one). If a change is mostly RED (deletions), STOP — that's a rebuild, forbidden.
# - NEVER touch a programmatic template lightly: editing one template changes hundreds of URLs at once.
#   Treat /industries/[industry], /malta/[location]/*, /aeo/* templates as high-blast-radius. Propose, never auto-apply.
# - When in doubt, propose the change and WAIT for approval. Do not write code in the first reply to a
#   non-trivial request — read, summarize what exists, propose, then build on approval.

# ============================================================
# LAW #2 — THE DOCTRINE: THREE HEROES x FOUR GATES  (HOW EVERY PAGE IS BUILT)
# ============================================================
# Full version in OARC-H360-BUILD-SPEC.md Section 1. Summary that governs every page:
#
# THE THREE HEROES (decide WHAT to say — in strict order):
#   Hero 1 = the business owner (our customer): what MORE does this make/save him? (not what it DOES)
#   Hero 2 = the owner's customer (our customer's customer): what do they GAIN so they return to Hero 1?
#   Hero 3 = OARC (LAST): only after 1 and 2 are served do keywords/SEO/AEO/distribution come in.
#   Skip Hero 1 or 2 and the page collapses into "same but better, it integrates, bla bla" — FORBIDDEN.
#
# THE FOUR GATES (decide HOW to say it — every word, every element):
#   Gate 1 Google-rank: real keyword in first 100 words + H1/H2, correct headings, right schema, genuinely useful.
#   Gate 2 AI-cite: clear entities/relationships, a real Q&A block phrased as a person asks an AI, self-contained answer.
#   Gate 3 owner-thinks: his words for his pain, fear of losing + desire to be full, operator-to-operator, never agency-down.
#   Gate 4 owner-searches: title/H1 mirror the literal query, Malta-anchored, one page = one intent.
#
# THEN: Devil's Advocate (kill anything a generic agency could've written; hunt "same but better/it integrates/bla bla")
#       + Polish (punchy, short, confident, read aloud).
#
# THE UNIFIED LAW: decide WHAT by the three heroes in order; decide HOW by the four gates. Both must pass before shipping.

# ============================================================
# LAW #3 — VOICE & FORBIDDEN PHRASES
# ============================================================
# - Communication with the owner: simple, everyday language (his stated preference). No jargon at him.
# - Page voice: confident, peer-to-peer, operator-to-operator. Pain-first. Maltese-local, never generic-global.
# - The moat: OARC operates real Maltese venues (Louisiana Mama, Palino, Calli Bistro). Operators who market,
#   not marketers guessing at operations. Reflect this wherever truthful — it's the E-E-A-T / experience signal.
# - NO unprovable number guarantees ("100-300 customers/month" is the competitor's weakness, not ours — sell the METHOD).
# - FORBIDDEN PHRASES: obey lib/seo/phrase-blocklist.md (the banned AI-tell list, enforced by seo-gate.sh).
#   On top of it, never write: "same but better," "we also do this," "it integrates," "passionate about,"
#   "revolutionary," "cutting-edge," "best-in-class," "next-generation," "omnichannel," "synergy,"
#   "leverage" (as verb), "solutions" (as generic noun). If you write any, you failed Devil's Advocate before submitting.

# ============================================================
# LAW #4 — TRUTH
# ============================================================
# - Never fabricate reviews, ratings, client logos, or case-study numbers (EU consumer law + Malta is too small;
#   fakes get caught and de-indexed, working AGAINST the goal). Use real numbers only when they exist.
# - Real, shipped H360 products vs roadmap: present built products as live (QR menu/ORDER, STAMP, PASS, SEND,
#   kitchen display). Frame unbuilt ones as roadmap/capability — never claim 21 live products.
# - Reviews mechanic: never reward a Google review directly (Google strips them, profile gets penalized).
#   Reward engagement with our own feedback step, then invite a Google review with NO reward attached.

# ============================================================
# LAW #5 — RESPECT THE EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE & ARCHITECTURE
# ============================================================
# - The LOCKED 60-core-URL tier list lives in replit.md (Tier 1 pillars -> Tier 7 supports). Read it before any
#   SEO/content/redirect/page work. (.local/memory/core-url-rank.md is the fuller version if present.)
# - Stack: Next.js App Router + Vercel. Tailwind + Shadcn/ui. Framer Motion + ScrollReveal.
#   Type: Montserrat / Nunito Sans / EB Garamond per design_guidelines.md. DO NOT migrate stack or swap the design system.
# - Motion: Framer Motion + smooth scroll only. NO heavy GSAP/Theatre.js/3D shaders (kills crawl speed AEO depends on).
#   Every animation must reinforce a Hero 1 or Hero 2 outcome (map filling, reviews counting up) — never decoration.
# - The SEO gate (scripts/seo-gate.sh) and slug-collision 308 map (lib/seo/seoSets.ts) are CONTRACTS. Respect them.
#   Programmatic governance: /aeo/* (44), /industries/[industry] (19), /malta/[location]/* (~80) — follow programmatic-audit.md.
# - H360 hospitality content lives at /h360 as a subfolder cluster (see OARC-H360-BUILD-SPEC.md Section 3B), built on top
#   of the existing site, feeding the one domain's authority. Don't create a separate domain or duplicate the stack.

# ============================================================
# HOW YOU WORK WITH ME (CURSOR BEHAVIOR)
# ============================================================
# - READ before you WRITE. Cite file paths + line numbers for every claim. If you can't cite it, say "unclear — check at runtime."
# - One page / one thing at a time. Show a reviewable diff. Wait for approval on anything non-trivial.
# - Before suggesting any user-facing element, silently self-test: who is Hero 1, who is Hero 2, what does each gain?
#   If you can't answer each in one specific sentence, you haven't done the work — go deeper.
# - When unsure, ASK. replit.md + OARC-H360-BUILD-SPEC.md are the source of truth. Sahan is the final arbiter.
#
# These are not suggestions. They are the operating contract for this repository.
